  "notes": "{抜|ぬ}く is a transitive godan verb with multiple meanings.\n\nTRANSITIVITY PAIR:\n- {抜|ぬ}く (transitive): to pull out\n- {抜|ぬ}ける (intransitive): to come out, fall out\n\nCONJUGATION:\n- {抜|ぬ}かない (negative)\n- {抜|ぬ}きます (polite)\n- {抜|ぬ}いて (te-form)\n- {抜|ぬ}いた (past)\n\nMEANINGS AND EXAMPLES:\n1. Extract: {歯|は}を{抜|ぬ}く (pull a tooth), {草|くさ}を{抜|ぬ}く (pull weeds)\n2. Omit: {食事|しょくじ}を{抜|ぬ}く (skip a meal)\n3. Surpass: {記録|きろく}を{抜|ぬ}く (break a record)\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {手|て}を{抜|ぬ}く: to cut corners, slack off\n- {気|き}を{抜|ぬ}く: to let one's guard down\n- {群|ぐん}を{抜|ぬ}く: to stand out from the crowd\n- {骨|ほね}を{抜|ぬ}く: to take the backbone out (weaken)",
